## Guard domain-version deletion endpoints

Context: Domain-version deletion now uses the shared lifecycle policy at the
service boundary. Both loaded-domain and Settings routes forward the caller's
application role so builders cannot bypass the administrator-only guard.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Added guarded deletion orchestration with existence, status, loaded-version, latest-version, and minimum-version checks.
2. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   Added the loaded-domain version deletion endpoint and derived its registry folder from the active domain.
3. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   Preserved the Settings deletion endpoint while forwarding the caller role to the shared service policy.
4. tests/units/settings/test_settings_version_deletion.py
   Added service coverage for successful deletion and every guarded conflict.
5. tests/units/api/test_delete_version_endpoints.py
   Added route coverage for target and caller-role forwarding.

